{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta","id":1113278,"title":"Second Impegrium (and other NuWW thoughts on WtA)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-08T09:36:13-07:00","id":1113278,"title":"Second Impegrium (and other NuWW thoughts on WtA)","content":"So, I have heard (through the grapevine, please note) that in the new Werewolf, some of the tribes are planning to start a new Impegrium. This alone is utterly baffling to me for reasons that I will come to later. But given the videogame seems to gear towards garou versus humans, I think that is the general theme of the new edition.<br /> <br /> Now, something that I have always felt weird about, is that garou are judged by the Impegrium even in modern times. Mainly, because the impegrium took place so long ago that there weren't even tribes then, nevermind the fact that many human cultures then could have easily done the same had they the power the garou had.<br /> <br /> The difference between modern garou and the ones that started the impegrium is vast, and much of the modern Nation could not function in the world the Impegrium took place in.<br /> <br /> This is why the concept of the garou versus humans is so strange to me, so much of the tribes is based on their relations to humans and especially to their kinfolk. General tribes like Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia and Glass Walkers aside, having an Impegrium when your kinfolk are so widely spread and so tied to the human world would gut the whole Nation.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Nation isn't perfect and logical, but it isn't filled with entirely misantropic people, either. Given that the setting discusses things like colonialism and its effects on indigineous peoples, poverty and how homeless are seen and general conflict between tradition and the modern world, losing that would harm the setting a lot.<br /> <br /> Another thing that the set up makes me worried about, is the fact that it again could push the ecological issues and fighting for them back to Captain Planet levels. The issue in WtA has never been truly against -humans-, instead it is more what is pushing humanity to hurt nature. Tradition versus modern world alone is such an interesting discussion, because there is no right answer to it. Modern world offers a lot of benefits and such, but then again, if the cost is losing touch to your own culture, is it worth it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T10:54:10-07:00","id":1113290,"title":"","content":"I am not too worried about it. Stories need conflict and I think it isn't that much of a stretch to imagine hardliners looking around at the screwed up, Wyrm-ascendent world and drawing the conclusion that a neo-Impergium would be the right move. A lot less humans and all this corruption might be halted.<br /> <br /> It might be like the Apocalyptic scenario of the Red Talons, where they open up vents in the earth that will kill a bunch of humans. I don't think there are enough Garou for a 'standard' Impergium to work, even if the entirety of Garou society was 100% on board, which they aren't. I bet there will be some mystic plot device that makes such a thing possible. It will likely be a goal one of the political factions is working towards. I would also not be surprised if whatever method the proponents of the new Impergium implement involves not killing kinfolk","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T11:20:47-07:00","id":1113297,"title":"","content":"I think the idea will be werewolves deciding whether to go after human evils as much as the supernatural.<br /> <br /> You know, like Pentex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T12:44:45-07:00","id":1113327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1113290#post1113290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not too worried about it. Stories need conflict and I think it isn't that much of a stretch to imagine hardliners looking around at the screwed up, Wyrm-ascendent world and drawing the conclusion that a neo-Impergium would be the right move. A lot less humans and all this corruption might be halted.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Except that they've done this a lot, but it amounts to navel-gazing, because they don't have the means to strike back at all of their foes and accomplish this end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It might be like the Apocalyptic scenario of the Red Talons, where they open up vents in the earth that will kill a bunch of humans. I don't think there are enough Garou for a 'standard' Impergium to work, even if the entirety of Garou society was 100% on board, which they aren't. I bet there will be some mystic plot device that makes such a thing possible. It will likely be a goal one of the political factions is working towards. I would also not be surprised if whatever method the proponents of the new Impergium implement involves not killing kinfolk </div> </div> </div>Their Tribe Falls scenario, incidentally, has them deliver news of their plans to rouse tectonic spirits of eruption to the rest of the Garou Nation in a very up-front way. The Garou Nation then bands against them. Not canonical, to be sure, but it is in character still.<br /> <br /> Even Margrave Konietzeko personally condemned the move and fought against their plans. Konietzko, de facto leader of the tribe that decries humanity, in its own way, nearly as badly as the Red Talons do, based on an extensive catalog of its atrocities over the years and weighing them against what the Garou have done (see the 2nd edition player's guide).<br /> <br /> NB: Apocalypse notes that, while the coastal eruptions around tectonically unstable zones were devastating to those who lived there, the release of methane clathrates stored in coastal shelves was even more devastating, as the deposits de-gassed en masse and either acted as greenhouse gases or exploded and then acted as slightly less potent greenhouse gases.<br /> <br /> NB Additional: The Talons were driven to it when prion disease that a few inconsiderate Talons got from eating humans wiped out most of their kinfolk and began to threaten other wolves. Those humans gotta lay off those O'Tolley's BrainBurgers; it's much too literal brain food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T13:30:23-07:00","id":1113352,"title":"","content":"The Second Imperium is a stupid idea. There are probably as many Garou as there were during the First Imperium, but there are 150 times as many people and human technology is ten thousand years more advanced. That means that there are more mortals with Willpower 9+ (Delirium Immunity) than there were mortals back then, and they have access to automatic rifles. <br /> <br /> Back during the First Imperium, every Garou probably faced 66 immune mortals who were equipped with stone weapons. In the Second Imperium, each Garou would probably be facing 10,000 immune mortals with modern weapons. In addition, there are probably similar multiplications for the number of Changelings, Mages, and Vampires, and each group would probably oppose the Second Imperium for their own reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T15:38:18-07:00","id":1113420,"title":"","content":"I imagine in any Second Imperium, they'd attack with magic rather than claws.<br /> <br /> Summon the Doomsday Virus from Bacteria's Realm or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T18:44:14-07:00","id":1113493,"title":"","content":"You can't return humanity &quot;back to nature&quot; without eliminating 99% of us. The world just can't support that many humans in a hunter gatherer lifestyle. Even though modern werewolves can be pretty horrible, I can't see a large enough percentage of them supporting genocide enough to make that happen.<br /> <br /> If they did, though, they could probably cause a lot of trouble for humanity. Especially if you ignore the heavy hitters in other game lines. The biggest death toll wouldn't come from attacking humans with teeth and claws, it would come from destroying infrastructure, assassinations, sabotage, terrorism, and other activities that werewolves could pull off with near impunity. Of course, when humans start to fight back, they could really do some devastating things to werewolves too and they would have Pentex helping them. In fact, Pentex could present themselves as the savior a of humanity and, in some sense, they would be right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T19:55:33-07:00","id":1113506,"title":"","content":"Eh, even if you don't return humanity back to nature, killing a lot of us would probably make it easier for the Garou and Gaia.<br /> <br /> You know, if you don't destroy the world because murdering 50% of humanity is still going to probably free the wyrm and destroy the universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T20:07:34-07:00","id":1113508,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not sure what killing half of humanity will do on a spiritual level. But in the material world it will certainly militarize humanity on an unprecedented level. At that point, Wyrm cults could probably just openly reveal themselves to humanity and get tons of support if they're willing to offer their power and information to help fight Garou. <br /> <br /> Humanity's counterattack so could be pretty bad for Gaia too - like nuking forests where Garou might live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T22:07:41-07:00","id":1113591,"title":"","content":"Killing half of humanity only takes the population back fifty years. It would have minimal effect of the environment, as it would be the poorer half that would die, as the richer half could afford medicine and food. Since Africa is disproportionately poor, 90% of its population would die (and that would only be 30% of the casualties).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T22:36:18-07:00","id":1113602,"title":"","content":"I imagine &quot;The second Imperigum&quot; will be an excuse for why garou nation got kicked in the face and its all super local and divided up again as humanity fights back hard something something hunters something something technocracy.. you know a copy and past of the V5 shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T06:39:57-07:00","id":1113708,"title":"","content":"Yes, which means they will be ruining WtA like they are VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T12:44:03-07:00","id":1113828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1113708#post1113708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, which means they will be ruining WtA like they are VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think a KEY point we need to remember with NuWW is they're completely done with the idea of &quot;Separate&quot; canons. There is &quot;ONE&quot; world of Darkness. There will be a greater level of explicit integration between the lines. So I'm damned sure the whole Technocracy pushes the Second Inquisition stuff is coming down in Werewolf too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T12:52:10-07:00","id":1113832,"title":"","content":"While I am a supporter of a unified WoD, I do not like the way that they are going about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T13:47:23-07:00","id":1113865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1113828#post1113828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think a KEY point we need to remember with NuWW is they're completely done with the idea of &quot;Separate&quot; canons. There is &quot;ONE&quot; world of Darkness. There will be a greater level of explicit integration between the lines. So I'm damned sure the whole Technocracy pushes the Second Inquisition stuff is coming down in Werewolf too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for me that is a major strike against it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T13:57:08-07:00","id":1113871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1113865#post1113865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, for me that is a major strike against it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm all for it.<br /> <br /> However, the games got way way way too weird and stylistic so there was no way in hell they made sense together. I'm trying to figure out how they can put the genie back in the bottle there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T14:44:27-07:00","id":1113878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1113871#post1113871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm all for it.<br /> <br /> However, the games got way way way too weird and stylistic so there was no way in hell they made sense together. I'm trying to figure out how they can put the genie back in the bottle there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From the looks of Vampire, by putting it in a blender an liquifying it. Any extra content is thrown out.(See the Sabbat)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T16:57:18-07:00","id":1113941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1113878#post1113878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> From the looks of Vampire, by putting it in a blender an liquifying it. Any extra content is thrown out.(See the Sabbat)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooo, do tell.<br /> <br /> Do you have a link or discussion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T17:11:36-07:00","id":1113948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1113941#post1113941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oooo, do tell.<br /> <br /> Do you have a link or discussion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't find the link when the Berlin talk happened there was discussion of what 5e would be. That the Sabbat would have followed the Call to the &quot;east&quot; where the majorityo f serious elders went for the Gehenna wars. You can kind of see this in the mechanics of hunger as it could in no way be used for playing Sabbat but that isn't needed because they aren't in the game to start. The whole second Inquisition thing for Vampire which pushes things back so they can't be tech savy and all that.<br /> <br /> From what I can remember the 5e books will have a cam edition and Anarch Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T19:21:45-07:00","id":1113990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1113948#post1113948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I can remember the 5e books will have a cam edition and Anarch Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those will be the first two <i>setting books</i>, according to WW's talk at Berlin. I think the Sabbat and the Independents will come later and I think what the Sabbat's doing will be a major plot point. It'd be pretty stupid to throw out 2/3s of the game...<br /> <br /> Asid from that, yes it seems they'll go with a more isolated setting for 5e, at least for Vampire. I hope they won't take it to Requiem-level extreme, but to some extent it might be okay. Yes, the Second Impergium could be the catalizator for making Werewolf more isolated too, it's not that big of a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T20:22:26-07:00","id":1114011,"title":"","content":"While I do think it would be great fun to run a Project Mayhem-style W;tA game, where the combined efforts of Garou and Kinfolk seek to bring about a simultaneous physical and spiritual Apocalypse (using the biblical definition of the word) in the modern world, it just doesn't seem likely to get off the ground in any practical sense. Such a thing would require so much cooperation and coordinated effort among the Garou nation that they wouldn't even need interference from other supernaturals or Pentex to foul things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T20:28:18-07:00","id":1114013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1113990#post1113990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those will be the first two <i>setting books</i>, according to WW's talk at Berlin. I think the Sabbat and the Independents will come later and I think what the Sabbat's doing will be a major plot point. It'd be pretty stupid to throw out 2/3s of the game...</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't in the core. They aren't even bad guys who you run into. They are as much a part of V5 as we understand it as DA Vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Asid from that, yes it seems they'll go with a more isolated setting for 5e, at least for Vampire. I hope they won't take it to Requiem-level extreme, but to some extent it might be okay. Yes, the Second Impergium could be the catalizator for making Werewolf more isolated too, it's not that big of a stretch. </div> </div> </div>In Requiem the Caphony exists. There's no &quot;Vampire global society&quot; but there sure as hell are secret emails and dark net interactions, kindred using Celphones and texting. Stuff you 5e is trying to make impossible!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T13:43:23-07:00","id":1114258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1114013#post1114013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They aren't in the core. They aren't even bad guys who you run into. They are as much a part of V5 as we understand it as DA Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, I don't know what exactly will be in the core book, but I won't be surprised, if the specific sect-related things will be entirely in the setting books, since those will come out the same time with the core (which, I won't be surprised if will end up a very slim book, focused on almost entirely the rules). Aside for that, yes, I think and said it on the Vampire subforum that I don't think the handling of the Sabbat this way is a good idea. Them focusing on the Middle-East business? that could be a good plot. Entirely went over there, thus totally left out from the core game? No, I don't think that's a good way to do it. I could understand the possibility that they maybe want to go back to the premise of the original game under 1e, with just the Camarilla clans and the struggle between the Ivory Tower and the Anarchs, buuuut... As with the isolation thing, it seems to be too extreme at this point, from the meager info we'd got. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Requiem the Caphony exists. There's no &quot;Vampire global society&quot; but there sure as hell are secret emails and dark net interactions, kindred using Celphones and texting. Stuff you 5e is trying to make impossible! </div> </div> </div>First, if you meant &quot;my&quot; 5e, it's not &quot;mine&quot;. I have serious reservations about it, I just try to handle it fairly and not going into histerics about it.<br /> <br /> Second, yes, I think total isolation is silly and not good for the setting. More isolation? yes, that could work and be interesting. Total isolation, I just can't picture with all the tech knowledge and mystical resources the sects could muster.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T13:51:23-07:00","id":1114262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1114258#post1114258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Second, yes, I think total isolation is silly and not good for the setting. More isolation? yes, that could work and be interesting. Total isolation, I just can't picture with all the tech knowledge and mystical resources the sects could muster.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think you overtly play up the isolation of Requiem. Its probably EASIER to travel in Requiem than Masquerade. Its just the world is less homoginized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T14:01:24-07:00","id":1114270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1114262#post1114262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you overtly play up the isolation of Requiem. Its probably EASIER to travel in Requiem than Masquerade. Its just the world is less homoginized.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. Yes there are nomads, however, the game, especially 1e was mostly written on the assumption that vampires are staying in their cities and do local stuff. It even stressed that every city is entirely differently organized and there's precious little communication between them, if there's any at all. Damnation City outright said, if I remember correctly, that yes, this level of isolation is artificial, but deliberate and a core part of the game.<br /> <br /> Requiem just used the isolation like &quot;this is the mood we wanted to convey, so it's like simply that&quot;, and that enables things like more free electronic communications, but on the large picture it is the same isolation between cities. If you want to stress a reason, it's the lack of global organizations, though I never read a reasoning for the lack of them, in-setting-wise, it was mostly on the meta-level of &quot;because we wanted it this way.<br /> <br /> 5e seems to use the reasoning that communication became too dangerous and that caused the isolation. Yes, it's a bit different, but the end result is really close and, IMO, more akin to Requiem than WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 07-10-2017, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T16:09:17-07:00","id":1115285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1114270#post1114270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think so. Yes there are nomads, however, the game, especially 1e was mostly written on the assumption that vampires are staying in their cities and do local stuff. It even stressed that every city is entirely differently organized and there's precious little communication between them, if there's any at all. Damnation City outright said, if I remember correctly, that yes, this level of isolation is artificial, but deliberate and a core part of the game.<br /> <br /> Requiem just used the isolation like &quot;this is the mood we wanted to convey, so it's like simply that&quot;, and that enables things like more free electronic communications, but on the large picture it is the same isolation between cities. If you want to stress a reason, it's the lack of global organizations, though I never read a reasoning for the lack of them, in-setting-wise, it was mostly on the meta-level of &quot;because we wanted it this way.<br /> <br /> 5e seems to use the reasoning that communication became too dangerous and that caused the isolation. Yes, it's a bit different, but the end result is really close and, IMO, more akin to Requiem than WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Requiem 2e doesn't rely on this much isolation, and I can point to several supplements that don't rely on the kind of isolation you say is endemic to Requiem. The clanbooks, for example, do not rely on extreme isolation - there's a significant amount of cross-domain communication and even some degree of travel in them.<br /> <br /> Requiem 2e changed a lot of the assumptions that 1e was written under, and it's not really fair to try to impose 1e's assumptions on 2e. Vampire 5th edition does seem to promote a significantly greater degree of isolation than Requiem ever did, never mind Requiem 2e specifically.<br /> <br /> Edit: This is probably not the best place to have a Requiem vs. Masquerade argument, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T16:34:34-07:00","id":1115293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115285#post1115285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Requiem 2e doesn't rely on this much isolation, and I can point to several supplements that don't rely on the kind of isolation you say is endemic to Requiem. The clanbooks, for example, do not rely on extreme isolation - there's a significant amount of cross-domain communication and even some degree of travel in them.<br /> <br /> Requiem 2e changed a lot of the assumptions that 1e was written under, and it's not really fair to try to impose 1e's assumptions on 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple of points:<br /> <br /> - Yeah, VtR 2e curbed back a lot of things. More communication (though cities are still on their own and being their own particular worlds, so that's fairly close, to how WW want to handle that part, according to them), no fog of ages, etc. It changed a lot. That's fair and given time, the 1e things will fade into the past. Right now it's still the 1e feel of the game which is dominant in many minds, particularly those who took a look on it and didn't like it, especially because of those reasons. It takes time to overwrite things like Damnation City, which is praised even by WoD fans. So yes, it'd be more fair to say &quot;5e seems to more akin to VtR 1e than VtM&quot;, than VtR in general, VtR 2e is still not old enough or have enough books to shift the perception. When people are talking about it, they simply mostly mean 1e, that is just that simple. <br /> <br /> - The clanbooks, as I understand it, are from the very end of the 1e run, with heavy involvement from Rose and practically the predecessors of 2e, even canon for 2e. Honestly, they are more 2e n my eyes than 1e. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire 5th edition does seem to promote a significantly greater degree of isolation than Requiem ever did, never mind Requiem 2e specifically. </div> </div> </div>Errr, don't think so? There's still a Camarilla after all and the bigger networks of the more organized clans. But we'll see. anyway, I don't really like it, but it depends on the degree, I'd be okay with a moderate level of going more underground, but I don1t want nearly total isolation, I think that's very-very un-WoD-like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: This is probably not the best place to have a Requiem vs. Masquerade argument, though. </div> </div> </div>Agree, but I just couldn't resist, because it's interesting. Also I don't think it's a &quot;versus&quot; thing, it's not a which is better question, it's just a comparison.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T16:39:45-07:00","id":1115294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115293#post1115293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Errr, don't think so? There's still a Camarilla after all and the bigger networks of the more organized clans. But we'll see. anyway, I don't really like it, but it depends on the degree, I'd be okay with a moderate level of going more underground, but I don1t want nearly total isolation, I think that's very-very un-WoD-like.</div> </div> </div> </div>The adventure makes everything seem extremely isolated, especially with those new airport scanners that can identify Kindred and the characters unable to leave town without risking utter destruction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115293#post1115293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree, but I just couldn't resist, because it's interesting. Also I don't think it's a &quot;versus&quot; thing, it's not a which is better question, it's just a comparison.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As long as we're both on the same page wrt this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T16:56:43-07:00","id":1115300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115294#post1115294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The adventure makes everything seem extremely isolated, especially with those new airport scanners that can identify Kindred and the characters unable to leave town without risking utter destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's very concerning and I'm curious how widespread that'll be? I hope not too much and it was just for this module to that extent, to keep the characters in the city. I could envision it as an emergency shutdown, which is reasonable, because of the Anarch uprising in Berlin, which practically translated to the mundane world as wide-spread terrorist attacks. I hope the situation presented in the scenario, which is pretty much the day after the revolt and mayhem, is just an extreme outlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T17:03:32-07:00","id":1115303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115294#post1115294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The adventure makes everything seem extremely isolated, especially with those new airport scanners that can identify Kindred and the characters unable to leave town without risking utter destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that supposed to be indicative of the new atmosphere for the WoD or is it just a sort of bullying ST style?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T17:06:12-07:00","id":1115305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115300#post1115300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah that's very concerning and I'm curious how widespread that'll be? I hope not too much and it was just for this module to that extent, to keep the characters in the city. I could envision it as an emergency shutdown, which is reasonable, because of the Anarch uprising in Berlin, which practically translated to the mundane world as wide-spread terrorist attacks. I hope the situation presented in the scenario, which is pretty much the day after the revolt and mayhem, is just an extreme outlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought there were other indications beyond that, but I don't want to go digging for it now, so I'll go with that being where I'm getting the impression.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115303#post1115303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that supposed to be indicative of the new atmosphere for the WoD or is it just a sort of bullying ST style?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure the two are separable when it comes to the new WW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T17:10:55-07:00","id":1115306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115305#post1115305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought there were other indications beyond that, but I don't want to go digging for it now, so I'll go with that being where I'm getting the impression.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't think that copters with New Inquisition snipers circling downtown and checking points one every road from the city will be an everyday norm. After a major violent event, yeah, it's plausible.<br /> <br /> They mentioned that yes, there is more isolation, due to communication being unsafe, but the exact extent is still a question. In the adventure, other European cities got mentioned, but as far s I understand, the Berlin anarch revolt spread like a wildfire , so we don1t have details about the hows and whys at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 07-12-2017, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T18:41:13-07:00","id":1115324,"title":"","content":"I really do not like the change in setting and tone that the people at nWW are trying to push. It is like they are trying to tap into the strains of isolationism and xenophobia that are going through the EU and the USA right now. Elder Kindred should really be above such things because they have seen it, again and again, throughout the centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T19:27:41-07:00","id":1115340,"title":"","content":"I think elders would be even more isolationist and xenophobic, if things go south, because they have so much to loose and they are frequently selfish cowards with power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T03:33:24-07:00","id":1115458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115340#post1115340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think elders would be even more isolationist and xenophobic, if things go south, because they have so much to loose and they are frequently selfish cowards with power.</div> </div> </div> </div>IF things go by the MET book, there won't be many caerns left and umbra is now legit dangerous to be in. So, that venue of communication is out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T14:40:39-07:00","id":1115680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=