1115458#post1115458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IF things go by the MET book, there won't be many caerns left and umbra is now legit dangerous to be in. So, that venue of communication is out.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey guys, remember that vital soul of the world that you need to safeguard in order to defend existence? The one that's half part of you? Well, you can't go into it. See, it was a pain for us to use in LARP, and hey where are you going?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T15:27:47-07:00","id":1115700,"title":"","content":"I think I can safely speak for the majority of WtA fans and say WTF? I cannot think of anything that would be more of an insult to WtA players than to deny them the Umbra. It is just another piece of evidence that nWW (and Paradox) do not give a flip about the tabletop game or any gameline other than VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T16:49:10-07:00","id":1115715,"title":"","content":"Hey. Guys? <br /> Relax. Werewolf is not for at least a year. Let's just see where this Vampire thing is going first. Not sure if judging all of it before release is the best option","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T17:10:46-07:00","id":1115717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115715#post1115715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey. Guys?<br /> Relax. Werewolf is not for at least a year. Let's just see where this Vampire thing is going first. Not sure if judging all of it before release is the best option</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure the MET Werewolf book is going to be a 1 on 1 indication for W5? V5 won't follow the MET Vampire metaplot, as far as I know. On the other hand, that was finished before the Paradoy buyout and they said BNS's Werewolf got a lot of input from WW, if I remember correctly, so, I dunno, we'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T22:46:14-07:00","id":1115810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115717#post1115717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure the MET Werewolf book is going to be a 1 on 1 indication for W5? V5 won't follow the MET Vampire metaplot, as far as I know. On the other hand, that was finished before the Paradoy buyout and they said BNS's Werewolf got a lot of input from WW, if I remember correctly, so, I dunno, we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between that and the constant banging of the ecoterrorist drum over the monster that defends the spirit world drum, I don't have high hopes. Or low hopes, even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T01:16:05-07:00","id":1115841,"title":"","content":"BNS werewolf is practically unrecognizeable Gifitiplines, werewolves now functioning like wererats etc..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T06:44:44-07:00","id":1115926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115303#post1115303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that supposed to be indicative of the new atmosphere for the WoD or is it just a sort of bullying ST style?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its Erickson we are talking about here so i am gonna bet the later. The man is mockingly called Dracula for a reason.<br /> <br /> As for the Impergrium. The way i see it the plot point is not about bringing back the impergrium but instead separating the Garou nation into two faction. The good tribes and the asshole tribes. Putting the impergrium back introduces the problem of lifting the veil one way or another and i doubt the wanna go that way for the now ONE world of darkness.<br /> <br /> Instead using the excuse of the second impergrium to separate the nation it makes things more morally simpler and foments the Furry Captain planet stereotype that Apocalypse has have to fought for a long time.<br /> <br /> See in previous iterations of Werewolf the Garou nation was problematic. It was awful and incompetent and retrograde to a point uselessness. It had a good goal to be sure, saving the world is as good as a goal as it can exist but carrying that goal were people with lots of conflicting moralities.<br /> <br /> You could play the most pure hearted Ma-ti planeteer but you would have to fight alongside a Red talon that believes in killing human children is the way to go for the nation or even a perfectly heroic Silver Fang that saves your life in battle, agrees with your on the main goal and methods to fight the wyrm but he happens to think &quot;consent&quot; is an after thought on his relationship with his mate on the matter of reproduction. Or a perfectly specimen of the fianna who just think that your packmate who is a metis should be &quot;put out of his misery&quot;.<br /> <br /> It was that contrast that really helped to give nuance to the game. Everything wasnt just black and white. The main enemy wasnt the cartoonishly evil pentex or BSDs but the nation itself that you hate to fight, compromise or just tolerate to begin to fight that cartoonishly evil bad guy. Its the adult sad moment when you found a group, cause or even political party you agree with and then find that it also houses people that take things too far or just are awful people that happen to agree with you. Its a complex thing to be sure, you cant really deshumanize them entirely because on a certain level they are you. You have common ground and you need them in some way or another.<br /> <br /> Not so much with the new divide. Now the schism has shove the problematic tribes into the Sanctum of Gaia and the &quot;good&quot; tribes into the Concordat of Stars. Now any moral complexity is gone from the Nation which each faction in their own echo chamber with concordat being obviously the PC choice being able to just point out to the Sanctum as the &quot;Other&quot;, the &quot;bad apples&quot; and then self-appoint themselves as the &quot;good tribes&quot; with the setting more or less agreeing with the statement when the harsh reality of the setting comes to question morally dubious actions. And truly now reducing the setting moral complexity to &quot;Furry Captain planet&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 07-14-2017, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T09:09:45-07:00","id":1115972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115926#post1115926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its Erickson we are talking about here so i am gonna bet the later. The man is mockingly called Dracula for a reason.<br /> <br /> As for the Impergrium. The way i see it the plot point is not about bringing back the impergrium but instead separating the Garou nation into two faction. The good tribes and the asshole tribes. Putting the impergrium back introduces the problem of lifting the veil one way or another and i doubt the wanna go that way for the now ONE world of darkness.<br /> <br /> Instead using the excuse of the second impergrium to separate the nation it makes things more morally simpler and foments the Furry Captain planet stereotype that Apocalypse has have to fought for a long time.<br /> <br /> See in previous iterations of Werewolf the Garou nation was problematic. It was awful and incompetent and retrograde to a point uselessness. It had a good goal to be sure, saving the world is as good as a goal as it can exist but carrying that goal were people with lots of conflicting moralities.<br /> <br /> You could play the most pure hearted Ma-ti planeteer but you would have to fight alongside a Red talon that believes in killing human children is the way to go for the nation or even a perfectly heroic Silver Fang that saves your life in battle, agrees with your on the main goal and methods to fight the wyrm but he happens to think &quot;consent&quot; is an after thought on his relationship with his mate on the matter of reproduction. Or a perfectly specimen of the fianna who just think that your packmate who is a metis should be &quot;put out of his misery&quot;.<br /> <br /> It was that contrast that really helped to give nuance to the game. Everything wasnt just black and white. The main enemy wasnt the cartoonishly evil pentex or BSDs but the nation itself that you hate to fight, compromise or just tolerate to begin to fight that cartoonishly evil bad guy. Its the adult sad moment when you found a group, cause or even political party you agree with and then find that it also houses people that take things too far or just are awful people that happen to agree with you. Its a complex thing to be sure, you cant really deshumanize them entirely because on a certain level they are you. You have common ground and you need them in some way or another.<br /> <br /> Not so much with the new divide. Now the schism has shove the problematic tribes into the Sanctum of Gaia and the &quot;good&quot; tribes into the Concordat of Stars. Now any moral complexity is gone from the Nation which each faction in their own echo chamber with concordat being obviously the PC choice being able to just point out to the Sanctum as the &quot;Other&quot;, the &quot;bad apples&quot; and then self-appoint themselves as the &quot;good tribes&quot; with the setting more or less agreeing with the statement when the harsh reality of the setting comes to question morally dubious actions. And truly now reducing the setting moral complexity to &quot;Furry Captain planet&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>People who don't like Werewolf will find reasons to be insultingly dismissive of it, even with all the work done, because they want to be insultingly dismissive. The bigger problem is how there was absolutely no indication of anything like the split or reinstatement of an Impergium would ever happen. The former seems to just be doing it for the sake of doing it, like no one was paying attention to why the Stargazers left and just wanted everyone to leave the clubhouse so that they could have a Cam and Sabbat for Werewolf (we already had the Garou Nation, Beast Courts and Ahadi, though, so splitting one of the existent 3 into 2 is even more questionable).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T10:05:33-07:00","id":1116004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115810#post1115810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Between that and the constant banging of the ecoterrorist drum over the monster that defends the spirit world drum, I don't have high hopes. Or low hopes, even.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be fair, I'm totally not against bringing back enviromentalism more to the forefront. It got a bit neglected under W20, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 07-14-2017, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T10:11:31-07:00","id":1116007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115926#post1115926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its Erickson we are talking about here so i am gonna bet the later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder how much of his players felt him (or WW in general) bullying them? For example on the big WoD LARPs recently? I didn't see anyone saying anything about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The man is mockingly called Dracula for a reason. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, because he posed for V20...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T10:37:41-07:00","id":1116021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116004#post1116004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To be fair, I'm totally not against bringing back enviromentalism more to the forefront. It got a bit neglected under W20, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The opening comic was about how fracking was going to be used to stir up a giant gribbly monster. Environmentalism is a major component of Werewolf, but in this specific use it tends to mix together in a way that makes the metaphorical literal and the future consequences much closer. This distinction is likely to be shorn from the game's design by WW, much as how the V5 pre-alpha ended up with a boring, railroady monofocus on one theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T11:09:59-07:00","id":1116027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115972#post1115972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People who don't like Werewolf will find reasons to be insultingly dismissive of it, even with all the work done, because they want to be insultingly dismissive. The bigger problem is how there was absolutely no indication of anything like the split or reinstatement of an Impergium would ever happen. The former seems to just be doing it for the sake of doing it, like no one was paying attention to why the Stargazers left and just wanted everyone to leave the clubhouse so that they could have a Cam and Sabbat for Werewolf (we already had the Garou Nation, Beast Courts and Ahadi, though, so splitting one of the existent 3 into 2 is even more questionable).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Concordat IS practically the Beast Courts. They are built upon &quot;returned&quot; Stargazers who brought Kitsune with them and readily allow non Garou Changing Breeds in their Genre. That they could have just had &quot;More and more garou up and leave to join the Beast Courts with their Stargazer friends&quot; would have basically doen the same thing.<br /> <br /> One thing I DID like though was completely dropping the Kitsune Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T11:50:04-07:00","id":1116042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1115972#post1115972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who don't like Werewolf will find reasons to be insultingly dismissive of it, even with all the work done, because they want to be insultingly dismissive. The bigger problem is how there was absolutely no indication of anything like the split or reinstatement of an Impergium would ever happen. The former seems to just be doing it for the sake of doing it, like no one was paying attention to why the Stargazers left and just wanted everyone to leave the clubhouse so that they could have a Cam and Sabbat for Werewolf (we already had the Garou Nation, Beast Courts and Ahadi, though, so splitting one of the existent 3 into 2 is even more questionable).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all people who think Werewolf is &quot;furry captain planet&quot; will hold that position regardless of evidence to the contrary. I know i didn't, the game put me off for years because people keep referring to it as &quot;Furry Captain Planet&quot; and because of reading actual plays/people talking about how they ran the game which boiled down to &quot;Furry Captain Planet&quot; . The only reason i gave it a chance was because W20 awesome character portraits with the actual text being deeper than that and showed nuanced of a deeper game....when handled correctly. The setting as presented now? Not a chance, it would have disproven my notion.<br /> <br /> What i mean is, there are potential players that are on the fence on werewolf and their conception of the game is hearsay because reading a 300+ book see if one likes it is too much work when one can just ask a trusted friend in the same hobbie or ask in a forum. Apocalypse cannot control the hearsay directed to them by other people but it shouldn't just embrace its negative stereotypes to become the game people accused it of being.<br /> <br /> Obviously the context of LARP NPC/PC ratio vs the one in Tabletop games is way different but that type of differentiation seems beyond NWW ability do distinguish at this point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116004#post1116004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, I'm totally not against bringing back enviromentalism more to the forefront. It got a bit neglected under W20, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally environmentalism was and is unimportant to Werewolf (the game itself), it just as well be replace with saving baby seals or any other objectively good goal. Its function is of a noble goal to showcase how Noble goal doesnt equal righteousness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116007#post1116007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how much of his players felt him (or WW in general) bullying them? For example on the big WoD LARPs recently? I didn't see anyone saying anything about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is the tale of the claustrophobic larper who got shove into a closet by him if you wanna run the rumor treadmill. But on the move itself, it was common tacky move of inexperience DMs (ala rocks falls everyone dies) of masquerade that when player either fed up with the politics of the city or there was any problem they try to bail on the city, said master would say &quot;Okay fine, your character then gets eaten by werewolves because..... they are werewolves 24/7 outside of the city with nothing better to do than kill pesky pc....erm i mean vampires who dont play ball&quot;<br /> <br /> Where i live south america, its kinda a meme at this point of classic dm dick moves.<br /> <br /> As for the LARP? Who cares? If Erickson only creds is organizing LARPs then that sadly is not enough to give me confidence. My experience with LARPs is that LARPS Dms are not game designers, i meet a few and are cool people of course but big bunch are only good at building echo chambers to themselves of players who happens to love their style with said players becoming sycophants to them as to deflect any kind of criticism, constructive or otherwise. LARPs scene (again, my experience) is about managing cliques and egos. Even if give the most generous of interpretations and say &quot;its about telling a story&quot; (and to be fair i have meet good LARPs DMs), its also more about managing personal storylines and not about building setting/mechanics.<br /> <br /> To be clear, what you are saying &quot;His players in the larp of Berlin seem happy&quot; doesn't mean much. How many of those players are Erickson close friends, how many are sycophants to him or just to Masquerade in general? Talent aside, because for all the praise he gather from his fanbase he has yet to actually produce something besides 2 rushed app games and 1 fiction, the other quality in which he can prove himself is in his ability to take and learn from criticism which he utterly lacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116007#post1116007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, because he posed for V20...</div> </div> </div> </div>Partially yes but not exactly. People mockingly call him Dracula because he project a professional image of what many people consider an edgelord. Its not even insulting at this point because Erickson fully embrace the label (or its unaware of the image he projects) with both his demeanor and actions. Just go to 4chan or even RPG.net.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":".  Clarifications 07-14-2017, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T11:59:26-07:00","id":1116048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116021#post1116021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The opening comic was about how fracking was going to be used to stir up a giant gribbly monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Environmentalism is a major component of Werewolf, but in this specific use it tends to mix together in a way that makes the metaphorical literal and the future consequences much closer. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I didn't read all the W20 books, but so far, I felt it got quite the backseat, behind other themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T14:13:49-07:00","id":1116107,"title":"","content":"For the good vs bad tribes, I find it interesting how the writers chose to make the Red Talons into basically the MAJOR bad guys within the Nation, rather than a splinter faction of isolatonists. They now officially ally with a faction known for torture and make special human killing squads. Fenrir got to be racist again, Furies accept males and poor Fianna are stuck with that one story justifying all the metis abuse. Wendigo join in because ??.<br /> <br /> For what it is worth, I don't mind the split, but it was not done to flesh out the tribes more. If anything, it seems to have been done only to split traditional vs modern garou.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T15:02:56-07:00","id":1116122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116048#post1116048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that's true.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, I didn't read all the W20 books, but so far, I felt it got quite the backseat, behind other themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that it was integrated with everything instead of being set out aside everything else. Everyone's aims are going to involve it in some part, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T15:06:12-07:00","id":1116124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116042#post1116042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally environmentalism was and is unimportant to Werewolf (the game itself), it just as well be replace with saving baby seals or any other objectively good goal. Its function is of a noble goal to showcase how Noble goal doesnt equal righteousness.</div> </div> </div> </div>We could agree to disagree on that. The enviromentalism angle was what I loved in WtA at the first sight. See, that's my pet peeve, instead of social and identity stuff, so it's important to me, for WtA to being WtA. I missed it dearly from WtF and while other NWoD lines had things I liked, WtF left me completely cold. NWoD fans tend to highly dislike the Changing Breeds supplement and you know what? I actually liked that a lot more than WtF, because it was a lot more like WtA for me. We're all different.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, there is the tale of the claustrophobic larper who got shove into a closet by him if you wanna run the rumor treadmill. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was brought up frequently lately, but I know practically nothing about it. Since he's doing Nordic LARPs, in that context, I'd want to know if it was consensual with the player, either right when it happened, or if the player agreed to such things as a part of the game? Maybe he/she even asked for it, to push his/her own boundaries, I don't know. The WW guys make a big deal about consent on their LARPs, like CoT and nobody made any complaint I saw about them, so it's jsut hard to me to imagine him as an abusive GM, or even person. I didn't get that impression, but I might add, I didn't speak with him personally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But on the move itself, it was common tacky move of inexperience DMs (ala rocks falls everyone dies) of masquerade that when player either fed up with the politics of the city or there was any problem they try to bail on the city, said master would say &quot;Okay fine, your character then gets eaten by werewolves because..... they are werewolves 24/7 outside of the city with nothing better to do than kill pesky pc....erm i mean vampires who dont play ball&quot;<br /> <br /> Where i live south america, its kinda a meme at this point of classic dm dick moves. </div> </div> </div>Come on, it was a tool to keep the players in the city and on the plot. Yes it's very cheap, even clich\u00e9d and railroady as hell, but it was just a playtest. I never heard that any of their games were like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the LARP? Who cares? If Erickson only creds is organizing LARPs then that sadly is not enough to give me confidence. My experience with LARPs is that LARPS Dms are not game designers, i meet a few and are cool people of course but big bunch are only good at building echo chambers to themselves of players who happens to love their style with said players becoming sycophants to them as to deflect any kind of criticism, constructive or otherwise. LARPs scene (again, my experience) is about managing cliques and egos. Even if give the most generous of interpretations and say &quot;its about telling a story&quot; (and to be fair i have meet good LARPs DMs), its also more about managing personal storylines and not about building setting/mechanics. </div> </div> </div>I'm not a LARPer, but I think yes, interpersonal connections and drama are far more important there, it seems to be just the nature of the thing. Otherwise and despite your assessment, I care, because their LARPs and how people enjoyed them and what they thought about them is a far more direct indicator at this point about how they write story, what they think about payer agency, what kind of characters they prefer in their games, etc. than this playtest. It's a bigger pool of examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To be clear, what you are saying &quot;His players in the larp of Berlin seem happy&quot; doesn't mean much. How many of those players are Erickson close friends, how many are sycophants to him or just to Masquerade in general? </div> </div> </div>If I'm right, it was an event with a couple hundreds of attendees... It's a little rude to dismiss all of them as sycophants and only-Masquerade fans. The folks from Darker Days Radio were here and enjoyed it immensely, as far as I understand, despite having a not very good predisposition about WW due to the ZackS thing. So yeah, it's still a slight galnce from without at my part, but it seems they know what they're doing, at least on that field.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Talent aside, because for all the praise he gather from his fanbase he has yet to actually produce something besides 2 rushed app games </div> </div> </div><i>He </i>didn't produce that. WW <i>licensed</i> those. He didn't wrote a word for those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and 1 fiction, the other quality in which he can prove himself is in his ability to take and learn from criticism which he utterly lacks. </div> </div> </div>Didn1t read it so far, so I won't judge it beforehand.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Partially yes but not exactly. People mockingly call him Dracula because he project a professional image of what many people consider an edgelord. Its not even insulting at this point because Erickson fully embrace the label (or its unaware of the image he projects) with both his demeanor and actions. Just go to 4chan or even RPG.net. </div> </div> </div>Which shows me that he has humor, which is good. People call him that mockingly, okay, let's embrace it and take it one step further! I find it amusing, but I like sarcasm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 07-14-2017, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T15:10:13-07:00","id":1116126,"title":"","content":"It's absolutely clear: most of the vocal opponents of NuWW will go to absolutely every lenght to crush the image of the new games.<br /> Should Martin Ericksson go to Africa to help starving children, he will surely get accused of trying to eat them while everyone is distracted.<br /> The most absurd claims I've read so far:<br /> 1) NuWW doesn't interact with fans, but when they ask for public feedback they are unprofessional because things.<br /> 2) Ericcson is evil because he LARPs: he is also the most abusive guy ever and he supports every kind of abuse, although he comes from Nordic LARP, which is the most politically correct kind of RP ever invented.<br /> 3) LARP is evil because things.<br /> 4) A one shot convention adventure heralds extensive ST railroading in the new edition because an introductory adventure meant to test the system should have been an open world sandbox story<br /> 5) Products from BNS are indicative of NuWW's hate of every game because things<br /> 6) WOD Gipsy is abominable racism but if NuWW wants to give Europeans a game where Amsterdam is not located in Denmark then they are disconnected from US players<br /> 7) Old WOD was some sort of game safe for 8yrs old kids ,while NuWW is EDGY because of an ambiguous pregen PC who might have been a paedophile (or not)<br /> 8) HUNDREDS of players at Berlin, Cologne, Grand Masquerade and Scandinavia are all lumped into the &quot;sycophants&quot; category, while a bunch of OP forumites who write over and over the same message all over the place should be considered as representative of the hobby<br /> 9) Minute details who are put there as possibilities to be explored are considered the DEFINITE mechanic or setting variation, magnified to ridicolous dimensions and used to animate abusive threads against EEEVIL NuWw<br /> <br /> There's such an enormous amount of vitriol that discussing these subjects has become not just impossible, but also really boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 07-14-2017, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T15:14:50-07:00","id":1116129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116122#post1116122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel that it was integrated with everything instead of being set out aside everything else. Everyone's aims are going to involve it in some part, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say &quot;integrated with everything else&quot;, I say &quot;it somewhat take a backseat&quot;. Yes it's a part of everyone's goals but also yes, it didn't get set aside as a primary theme on itself. I don't dispute that it's still an important part of the setting, I just say that I preferred when it was more central. Honestly, I feel somewhat like that about our real world too. Today, everything is clean and green and sustainable and other cool labels, but actually we're speaking a lot less about environmental destruction than a decade or two ago. We don't care as much, because we think things are a lot better and we're complacent and content, because we feel we're doing things right. But I deride, sorry, it's just really my pet peeve and also my profession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T15:31:42-07:00","id":1116134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116124#post1116124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We could agree to disagree on that. The enviromentalism angle was what I loved in WtA at the first sight. See, that's my pet peeve, instead of social and identity stuff, so it's important to me, for WtA to being WtA. I missed it dearly from WtF and while other NWoD lines had things I liked, WtF left me completely cold. NWoD fans tend to highly dislike the Changing Breeds supplement and you know what? I actually liked that a lot more than WtF, because it was a lot more like WtA for me. We're all different.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, that was brought up frequently lately, but I know practically nothing about it. Since he's doing Nordic LARPs, in that context, I'd want to know if it was consensual with the player, either right when it happened, or if the player agreed to such things as a part of the game? Maybe he/she even asked for it, to push his/her own boundaries, I don't know. The WW guys make a big deal about consent on their LARPs, like CoT and nobody made any complaint I saw about them, so it's jsut hard to me to imagine him as an abusive GM, or even person. I didn't get that impression, but I might add, I didn't speak with him personally.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Come on, it was a tool to keep the players in the city and on the plot. Yes it's very cheap, even clich\u00e9d and railroady as hell, but it was just a playtest. I never heard that any of their games were like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not a LARPer, but I think yes, interpersonal connections and drama are far more important there, it seems to be just the nature of the thing. Otherwise and despite your assessment, I care, because their LARPs and how people enjoyed them and what they thought about them is a far more direct indicator at this point about how they write story, what they think about payer agency, what kind of characters they prefer in their games, etc. than this playtest. It's a bigger pool of examples.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If I'm right, it was an event with a couple hundreds of attendees... It's a little rude to dismiss all of them as sycophants and only-Masquerade fans. The folks from Darker Days Radio were here and enjoyed it immensely, as far as I understand, despite having a not very good predisposition about WW due to the ZackS thing. So yeah, it's still a slight galnce from without at my part, but it seems they know what they're doing, at least on that field.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>He </i>didn't produce that. WW <i>licensed</i> those. He didn't wrote a word for those.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Didn1t read it so far, so I won't judge it beforehand.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which shows me that he has humor, which is good. People call him that mockingly, okay, let's embrace it and take it one step further! I find it amusing, but I like sarcasm.</div> </div> </div> </div>AMEN ! I agree on everything you have written !!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T18:00:14-07:00","id":1116180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116124#post1116124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm right, it was an event with a couple hundreds of attendees... It's a little rude to dismiss all of them as sycophants and only-Masquerade fans. The folks from Darker Days Radio were here and enjoyed it immensely, as far as I understand, despite having a not very good predisposition about WW due to the ZackS thing. So yeah, it's still a slight galnce from without at my part, but it seems they know what they're doing, at least on that field.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow okay let me clarify this before it goes out of hand. I am NOT Accusing or dismissing people who like the event as sychopants. What i tried to convey was that a unfortunate big part of larp is about the st ability of building echo chambers and managing egos. And that the success of erickson in managing an event is not an indication of his ability of producing good mechanics/setting.<br /> <br /> In the same vein the organizing the anual plumber convention doesnt necesarily mean one is a great plumber. It just mean one is good at organizing events","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T18:12:25-07:00","id":1116184,"title":"","content":"That's fair, but I think it's still a good indicator about the things I wrote. What kind of characters they want to encourage, what kind of stories, how they envision the setting, how they wove a story, how much agency they give to players, how they handle controversial things. <br /> <br /> Those are quite important things and unfortunately, the TT community's bigger part (including me) don1t know details about them (and it's WW's fault too, that we don't). To make up a fair picture, I'd like to hear people who played in their games, probably with them as fellow players, or STs, or just spoken with them face-to-face.<br /> <br /> Also, I think there's trutha in what you're saying about LARP echo chambers, based on what I heard from friends, but I don't think that's the case in this case, considering we're speaking about multiple international events with hundreds of attendees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T20:17:35-07:00","id":1116222,"title":"","content":"The thing is that we do not have to buy W5 (or V5, C5, etc) if we do not like the mechanics and/or the setting. There is nothing that has been said about the mechanics (assuming they reflect the mechanics of V5) or the setting (really, why would anyone want to play WtA without the Umbra?) that makes old WtA fans like me want to pay a cent for the nWW games. The great thing is that we have four good editions of books (W20, WtA Revised, WtA 2e, and WtA 1e) to fall back upon and we do not need to buy anything made by nWW unless they actually get their heads out of their rear ends and listen to the WtA tabletop fans.<br /> <br /> Now, nWW has enough time to reverse track on the mechanics and the setting, and I really hope that they do change their mind so something positive comes out of this mess, but I do not need to buy their products to get my WtA fix. Anyway, it is not like they are really White Wolf, they are just a reanimated corpse of White Wolf created by Paradox so that Paradox could promote the IP in order to make money off licensing video games and television shows from the IP. In fact, the closest thing to the old White Wolf is OPP from what I understand, which is why I do not understand what Paradox is doing. They should have just asked OPP to do the 5th edition as a unified WoD and benefited from having competent people, many of whom who worked for the old WW, doing the gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T21:02:56-07:00","id":1116230,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116124#post1116124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come on, it was a tool to keep the players in the city and on the plot. Yes it's very cheap, even clich\u00e9d and railroady as hell, but it was just a playtest. I never heard that any of their games were like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is the thing, if he is so good a DMing, then why resort to the most cliche, cheap and railroady for a path that is largely unnecessary? If this is a scenario to test the mechanics then the players chossing to bail is a moot point, one assumes that if a gather my friends to test this mechanics in the scenarios we would do it. But if they wrote the pregen PCs one has to play with they might as well put some motivation for the PC to not leave.<br /> <br /> But to be fair its a minor complain. I was responding to a question of whether &quot;Lupines are gonna eat you as soon as you leave the city&quot; is a GM bullying style and it is. Is the WoD equivalent of rocks fall everyone dies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116126#post1116126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's absolutely clear: most of the vocal opponents of NuWW will go to absolutely every lenght to crush the image of the new games.</div> </div> </div> </div>NuWW doesnt need help to crush its own image, they are doing a fine job at that on their own sadly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116126#post1116126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Martin Ericksson go to Africa to help starving children, he will surely get accused of trying to eat them while everyone is distracted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really wish he would go to Africa to feed children instead of making games to be honest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116126#post1116126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most absurd claims I've read so far:</div> </div> </div> </div>On the same vein, the most absurd defenses of NWW i have read have been:<br /> 1) People defend their shitty PR with the excuse that other companies also have shitty PR.<br /> 2) When people complain that the playtest feel rushed, bad, incomplete or raises to many mechanical question, defenders say that they shouldnt expect much from a playtest as its only there to test the mechanics.<br /> 3) When people complain that the pedophile vampire distract from testing the mechanics, defenders say people shouldnt complain because the playtest is there to more than just test the mechanics! Its there so they author can explore themes too!<br /> 4) There is no pedophile vampire because A) NuWW said so and B) Subtext stop becoming a thing when NuWW is involved.<br /> 5) The fact that NuWW approve the setting changes to By Night studios, multiple times mentioned a focus on LARP and a &quot;let go back to ecoterrorism&quot; comment on werewolf is NO indication that they might go this route because.....because.<br /> 6) Managing larps is the same as writting game mechanics......just like being a event organizer gives you expertise in all the types of convention one has manage because they all use the same sorts of skills. Is true though, thats why event organizers all fight each other to organize surgeon symposiums is either that or 7+ years of medical school to learn neurosurgery.<br /> 7) Any issue with the mechanic is either the person &quot;not getting it&quot; or &quot;not giving NuWW the benefit of the doubt&quot; which they obviously deserve since they did....that....thing.....the other day....with those guys....maybe.<br /> 8) OPP forums dont represent the apparent consumer base of NuWW, neither does RPG.net, neither does Reddit, neither does 4chan. Neither does any site that says bad things about NuWW. The consumer base is only the people who went to the larp in berlin and..... all that other consumer that exist in the world, that happens to not use internet but totally exist guys! Its like Shrodinger consumers that doesnt exist until one needs them to exclude elements from it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116126#post1116126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's such an enormous amount of vitriol that discussing these subjects has become not just impossible, but also really boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>One the same vein: There's such an potent shade of pink-glasses that discussing these subjects has become not just impossible, but also really boring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116107#post1116107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wendigo join in because ??.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that simple because the Garou nation is split now between the good progressive tribes and the asshole tribes.<br /> <br /> So now we have the human haters (Red talons), the racists (Fenrir, and fianna), the <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">misandrous (Black furies), ableist (Fianna again), the homophobics (Did someone said Fianna?) and the Xenophobic (Wendigo) are in a corner because thats how life works. All the bad people/people you disagree with are &quot;over there&quot; outside of your group and so they can never be you because they are different! </span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116222#post1116222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, it is not like they are really White Wolf, they are just a reanimated corpse of White Wolf created by Paradox so that Paradox could promote the IP in order to make money off licensing video games and television shows from the IP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets be fair here, the blame for this is not wholly on NuWW. Yes, they said yes to this changes but the idea was from By Night studios and they should carry the blame for this awful changes. There is a chance whoever small (winning the lottery 3 times in a row small) that they said yes to the changes because they would be only contained to the LARP of by night studios and nothing else. You know....i am a sucker for hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 07-15-2017, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T21:57:32-07:00","id":1116238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116230#post1116230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Lets be fair here, the blame for this is not wholly on NuWW. Yes, they said yes to this changes but the idea was from By Night studios and they should carry the blame for this awful changes. There is a chance whoever small (winning the lottery 3 times in a row small) that they said yes to the changes because they would be only contained to the LARP of by night studios and nothing else. You know....i am a sucker for hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>IF we are going to be fair none of the BNS Stuff has been said to be any more in W5 than W20 stuff. Onyxpath Werewolf stuff has come out after BNS' werewolf and hasn't been pushed to line up anymore than BNS' vampire. More We've seen previews of V5 and it takes NOTHING from BNS Vampire. It lines up mroe readily with v20 it just goes completely crazy from there. <br /> <br /> <br /> What we do know about W5. There will be a &quot;Second Imperigum&quot; on the table. The Werewolves will be treating Global warming as Gaia &quot;dying of Fever&quot; We know there will be extreme matching between the gamelines with them more heavily effecting each other. We know alot about how vampire is changed and that a Random Get of Fenris showing up as a &quot;Rocks fall everyone dies&quot; is an option of the players have teh audacity of trying to leave Berlin by just walking out. Werewolves apparently still have free Rage actions(even if its cut down like Celerity was so they could only use 2 extra a round)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T00:22:47-07:00","id":1116282,"title":"","content":"Weirdly, I shit you not, but in my W20 game, I decided to have a Civil War between the Garou Nations.<br /> <br /> I stole from Forsaken and had half become rabid fundamentalist nutjobs like the Pure and the other half become much more moderate good guy Albretch types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T02:48:00-07:00","id":1116309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116282#post1116282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weirdly, I shit you not, but in my W20 game, I decided to have a Civil War between the Garou Nations.<br /> <br /> I stole from Forsaken and had half become rabid fundamentalist nutjobs like the Pure and the other half become much more moderate good guy Albretch types.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, the idea isn't bad. But I highly prefer the split be more personal, as in some members of a tribe are moderate and some more eager to use horrible methods. After all, Shadow Lords are a tribe of garou who want to make right old wrongs.<br /> <br /> But they are also a tribe of garou who are willing to torture others for information.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T06:17:34-07:00","id":1116346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116238#post1116238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IF we are going to be fair none of the BNS Stuff has been said to be any more in W5 than W20 stuff. Onyxpath Werewolf stuff has come out after BNS' werewolf and hasn't been pushed to line up anymore than BNS' vampire. More We've seen previews of V5 and it takes NOTHING from BNS Vampire. It lines up mroe readily with v20 it just goes completely crazy from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont think thats true. When W20 was released there wasnt NuWW in existence yet. Same with MET: Vampire so they didnt had to get their material approved. <br /> <br /> At the time of MET: Werewolf, i did require NuWW revision &amp; approval of them. Same with the last W20 release &quot;Shattered Dreams&quot; was revisioned, changes required from NuWW and then approved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T07:19:23-07:00","id":1116372,"title":"","content":"And Shattered Dreams is not even canon...no, the idea of the Umbra not being accessible to Garou is something done to please the LARPing crowd because it is too difficult for them to game on two levels of reality. It is also something done to simplify video games and television shows, as it pretty much removes the Umbra from the video games and television shows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T07:44:21-07:00","id":1116381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116372#post1116372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Shattered Dreams is not even canon...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, it not being canon was one of the changes mandated by NWW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T07:59:25-07:00","id":1116389,"title":"","content":"Ah, that is interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T10:11:26-07:00","id":1116455,"title":"","content":"Ok, I have to ask....where are people getting the Fianna are homophobic (yet not the Get who state how unnatural homosexuality is in their revised tribe book), and racist from? I honestly had to miss those themes all these years (not going to touch the ablism....since I've ranted about that a bit on this site, I'm too aware of it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T10:23:50-07:00","id":1116459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116309#post1116309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, the idea isn't bad. But I highly prefer the split be more personal, as in some members of a tribe are moderate and some more eager to use horrible methods. After all, Shadow Lords are a tribe of garou who want to make right old wrongs.<br /> <br /> But they are also a tribe of garou who are willing to torture others for information.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amusingly, in my game, 2/3rds of the Silver Fangs joined the Pure and like 3 (out of the ENTIRE TRIBE) Shadow Lords joined the Pure. The Shadow Lords are the backbone of my Forsaken group because I didn't want a &quot;good guys vs. bad guys&quot; pure split.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T11:07:11-07:00","id":1116478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116346#post1116346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont think thats true. When W20 was released there wasnt NuWW in existence yet. Same with MET: Vampire so they didnt had to get their material approved.<br /> <br /> At the time of MET: Werewolf, i did require NuWW revision &amp; approval of them. Same with the last W20 release &quot;Shattered Dreams&quot; was revisioned, changes required from NuWW and then approved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Had to check the timeline, I was counting the backer release on BNS stuff, so i was wrong there. I still go with BNS Vampire changes have been completely ignored for V5 why should the BNS werewolf changes mean anything? Yes they were Nuww approved but much like how Shattered Dreams was made &quot;noncanon&quot; by said process BNS Werewolf was well underway before NuWW came in and may have required significant rewriting to bring it to what they wanted.<br /> <br /> We'll see in Changing Ways if any of the BNS Metaplot is referenced at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going to still stick with the NuWW has plenty of itsown Crazy to deal with it doesn't need BNS' stuff as well. And &quot;its harder to go into the umbra&quot; isn't even close to the craziest change in BNS. Every Changing breed functions like Ratkin. You bite someone and if they are kinfolk they might survive and change everyone else AUTO DIES. Gifts are now basically disciplines with &quot;in clans&quot; and everything!<br /> <br /> All Fera are dying.. except Kitsune who lost the curse and now are like super common(ok this i like!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T11:09:56-07:00","id":1116479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116455#post1116455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I have to ask....where are people getting the Fianna are homophobic (yet not the Get who state how unnatural homosexuality is in their revised tribe book), and racist from? I honestly had to miss those themes all these years (not going to touch the ablism....since I've ranted about that a bit on this site, I'm too aware of it)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've always thought the Nation was mildly Homophobic or at least included a &quot;Breeding is your duty&quot; thing. That there were all sorts of squicky bits that greyed up the whole thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T13:42:23-07:00","id":1116537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116479#post1116479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've always thought the Nation was mildly Homophobic or at least included a &quot;Breeding is your duty&quot; thing. That there were all sorts of squicky bits that greyed up the whole thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yea I can see the nation that way, heck w20 relate across the world had a lesbian silver fang and she talked about how her tribe hated it, I'm just lost as to how the Fianna are singled out here...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 07-15-2017, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T14:31:24-07:00","id":1116558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116479#post1116479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always thought the Nation was mildly Homophobic or at least included a &quot;Breeding is your duty&quot; thing. That there were all sorts of squicky bits that greyed up the whole thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an irony which makes quite a few people uncomfortable when you realize the Garou are a bunch of religious fundamentalist terrorists with a focus on forced breeding. Also, quite a few with anti-technology views. However, I have no problem with this because I played (and enjoyed) Warhammer 40K and that's a bunch of religious fundamentalist fascists.<br /> <br /> Like Vampire, you need to remember the Garou aren't the GOOD guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T14:34:54-07:00","id":1116559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116479#post1116479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've always thought the Nation was mildly Homophobic or at least included a &quot;Breeding is your duty&quot; thing. That there were all sorts of squicky bits that greyed up the whole thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which isn't surprising and, considering their status, not even illogical. I imagine it goes as it did in earlier ages. If you sired/birthed some progeny, then nobody cared what you did in your free time and who you truly loved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T14:38:19-07:00","id":1116560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116558#post1116558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's an irony which makes quite a few people uncomfortable when you realize the Garou are a bunch of religious fundamentalist terrorists with a focus on forced breeding. Also, quite a few with anti-technology views. However, I have no problem with this because I played (and enjoyed) Warhammer 40K and that's a bunch of religious fundamentalist fascists.<br /> <br /> Like Vampire, you need to remember the Garou aren't the GOOD guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but they aren't the bad guys either, at least not all of them. Also, they have a (serious) point, beside being selfish bastards, like vampires and arguably, mages. But yeah, a lot of them, maybe the majority aren't exactly progressive liberals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T15:03:24-07:00","id":1116566,"title":"","content":"Mind you, I actually have it brought up in my games that Pure Breed is a completely awful background as it is literally, &quot;People respect you because of racism.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T15:08:53-07:00","id":1116569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116566#post1116566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, I actually have it brought up in my games that Pure Breed is a completely awful background as it is literally, &quot;People respect you because of racism.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, partly, but it's also about lineage, arguably even more, which isn't the same as racism. They aren't respecting you because of the color of your fur, but because you could trace back your family tree to great heroes of the tribe. I know it's a quite alien and even abhorrent notion for modern western people and frankly, I'm not a fan of thinking like that, but nobility is a thing and it doesn't equal racism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T15:09:57-07:00","id":1116570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113278-second-impegrium-and-other-nuww-thoughts-on-wta?p=1116569#post1116569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, partly, but it's also about lineage, arguably even more, which isn't the same as racism. They aren't respecting you because of the color of your fur, but because you could trace back your family tree to great heroes of the tribe. I know it's a quite alien and even abhorrent notion for modern western people and frankly, I'm not a fan of thinking like that, but nobility is a thing and it doesn't equal racism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the way I remember it is even people who have no idea who their ancestors are can look like Pure Breed 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T15:11:39-07:00","id":1116571,"title":"","content":"Could be, I'm mostly working on W20 terms, after my memories and a quick scan, I don't know how it was in earlier editions.","signature":